Enhancement: Add experimental `restic protect` command and `--skip-object-locked` for `forget`/`prune`

Backups stored on S3-compatible storage could previously still be deleted by
anyone holding delete-capable credentials, even when a retention policy meant
to keep them. Restic now has experimental support for S3 Object Lock on the
`s3` backend. The new `restic protect --keep-* --for <duration>` command
extends Object Lock retention on the snapshots a retention policy currently
wants to keep, and on the data they need. `forget` and `prune` gained a
`--skip-object-locked` flag to skip snapshots and packs that are still
locked instead of failing the whole run. This requires an S3 bucket created
with Object Lock enabled and the `object-lock` experimental feature flag
(`RESTIC_FEATURES=object-lock`).

